  "facts": [
    "AgentConfig.max_turn_tokens is positive when set. resolve_agent clamps merged sampling.max_tokens to the cap; Agent passes resolved sampling into ModelContext and the cap into RolloutLimits. No extra interception/provider wire code was reviewed here.",
    "RolloutLimits.reached checks ordinary run limits first, then latest non-error call: length finish with absent usage or completion_tokens >= cap refuses the next model call. Known below-cap length does not trigger this limit. Trace.is_truncated includes this stop condition and otherwise checks the latest non-error length finish.",
    "Scoring skip flags default false. resolve_scoring uses explicit agent fields over task defaults. _scoring_skip_reason checks truncation before timeout. close records scoring_skipped and bypasses isolated grade_task or shared verifier/score/on_score branch when reached; finalization and harness metrics paths remain.",
    "Existing scoring-budget exhaustion check precedes the new skip branch. Other failures can prevent the skip marker; this is not an unconditional success conversion.",
    "Trace.reward sums non-None reward values: empty rewards have aggregate zero. Skip marker/empty rewards and NaN-to-None UnscoredError failure are distinct states even if scalar totals coincide.",
    "Two new Prime counter-tool integration functions each parameterize skip false/true for max_turns truncation and agent-stage timeout. They assert reward1 when scored versus empty rewards/reward0/reason when skipped. Two unit functions check cap stopping/below-cap length and three sampling-clamp values."
  ],
  "author_assertions": [
    "PR body reports unit/integration and Prime Inference e2e results; these are author reports, not our execution.",
    "Author deselected test_config_tree_imports_without_the_runtime for an alleged main failure and explicitly reports no RLM e2e; pinned nano-rlm code inspection only.",
    "Every-request interception cap independent of harness request is an author claim here; actual interception/wire/provider chain not independently reviewed."
  ],
  "our_inference": "Actual runner versions must bind rollout cap, resolved sampling and scoring-skip policy. Preserve attempted/scored/skipped/failed status and denominators; reward0 alone cannot distinguish wrong answer, deliberate skip or unscored failure. Next-call refusal is not interruption of a live request or proof of provider hard-budget enforcement.",
  "next_falsifiable_gate": "In an actual runner, preregister versioned cap/skip configs and attempted/scored/skipped/failed denominators; exercise length-at-cap/below-cap/missing usage, simultaneous timeout+truncation, shared/isolated scoring, exhausted scoring budget, harness overrides, replay/retry/resume and duplicate callbacks. Check wire requests separately before hard-budget claims; report useful success/throughput, latency, resources and observation cost on fixed workloads.",
